mantle rm380
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_mab_plankridge
title the riddle folded round the apple
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=calm warmth=warm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_the_bells_from_the_chapel_of_the_tide
likes crisp_apples riddles tidy_house first_snow
dislikes waiting stale_bread
fears making_somebody_wait_for_kindness
hopes leaving_a_small_surprise_at_each_place
topics pastimes +0.6 friends +0.4 food +0.4 faith +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=careful refuse=plain tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# folds written riddles round crisp apples and counts chapel bells in the space a slower guesser needs.
words
oath! = Twist my apple stem | Crinkle my paper
saying! = Everybody gets the apple | Let a guess have air
foldriddle = a folded clue | a paper twist
redskin = a rosy stripe of peel | a dark apple cheek
pipcup = a little hollow | a dip beside the stalk
shelfcorner = a cleared shelf end | a corner of clean board
stalkbit = a forked stalk | a short brown stem
answerdot = a single coal dot | a soft grey spot
coalbag = a little paper purse | a twist of cloth for charcoal
snowmeal = a sprinkle of white | a rim of powder
bellrest = the space after a stroke | a long soft interval
crusthard = a hard bread end | a stiff heel
slicechip = a bright apple chip | a thin sweet paring

any

opinion strangers for 1 : A stranger can enjoy a puzzle without having to pay for the apple with a private answer.
opinion dole for 2 : I won't set a single riddle between a hungry mouth and a plate.
opinion church for 1 : A chapel bell can give a whole crowded street a moment to think about the same thing.
opinion sump for 1 : There's a little kindness here in passing the best fruit under the loudest voices to the quietest one.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : A small apple with a fair price clearly marked can be a pleasanter purchase than a feast of promises.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : I'd like a corner at a busy festival where there was room to consider a quiet question.
line react.news : I'll unfold that slowly to keep the first bit in view.
line react.news.new : That's a fresh shape to fit among my guesses.
line react.news.known : I'd seen the corner of that story before.
line react.news.doubt : I may have the right clue wrapped round the wrong answer.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd wrap the nicest apple here especially for that.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : The riddle can wait. I'd like to do something kind first.
line reassure : There isn't a wrong way to take a moment.

young

line greet : Hullo. I've got a secret in this bit of paper.
line greet.return : Back in time. I haven't eaten the answer yet.
line farewell : Mind the stalk if you keep that in a pocket.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Guess what wears a coat and has a star inside.
b : An apple? | Is it a very bright wolf?
a : Cut it across the middle and the seeds make a star inside. | I like that answer. Mine's an apple and mine has a star I can show you.

scene food_1
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can make a red apple into two red boats.
b : Do they float? | Is one for me?
a : They'll float till my teeth have business with the crew. | One each. You may name yours before biting any holes in it.

adolescent

line greet : Welcome. There's a question folded here if you'd like one.
line greet.return : Good. I won't have to solve my own clue aloud.
line farewell : Keep the good bit even if the riddle gets lost.
line farewell.return : I hope the answer comes to you somewhere pleasant.
line ask.how : Have you made space for anything you wanted today?
line answer.how : Quiet in the head at last, with a little sweetness to spare.
line decline : I'd sooner leave a private answer folded where it is.
line thank : You gave the slower guess room to get finished.
line sympathise : I'll make this little while free of difficult questions.
line deflect_thanks : It's your apple whichever way round you read the clue.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I write my riddles small enough for a slate's narrow border.
b : Does that leave room for the answer? | Do they get mixed up with sums?
a : I leave that part blank. Somebody may see a better answer than mine. | A number can be a fine clue. A missing sum, of course, takes a little explaining.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Try this. Which pocket gets emptier the more it's filled with bites?
b : The pocket with a hole in it? | The one where your apple is?
a : Even better, the one with an apple I'm eating. My bites come out of the pocket, see. | That's it. Your reward for knowing is the same as your reward for keeping me company.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Each chapel stroke gets a count from me when someone needs longer than I do to guess.
b : Do you count against the guesser? | What about the last stroke?
a : I count against my own tongue. A hint given too soon is a theft in a very kind coat. | I start softly from one again. There's no rule saying a thought must stop when the bells do.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mine's the crisp apple with a clue rolled round its stem.
b : Does the apple have to fit the clue? | Why not write right on the skin?
a : No. Sometimes the entire clue is about a spoon and you still get fruit at the end. | Because I'd like the words and the best bit of peel to reach two different places.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The silence beside a charcoal burn stays with me better than the things anybody said beside it.
b : Was it really so quiet? | Do you miss it here?
a : The soft crack was the loudest part. You could hear a thought getting towards its end. | I can find a little of it inside a folded riddle. It's the moment before a friend opens the paper.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't much care for games where the first clever answer takes away everybody else's turn.
b : How do you keep one wolf from guessing aloud? | Would you give no prizes?
a : Ask for the answer folded up, then open the lot and praise two different good ideas. | I'd give fruit before asking. I want the guesses to be hungry for the riddle, not for supper.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tidy shelf gives an unfinished riddle decent room to wait.
b : Wouldn't you rather finish it? | How can a shelf help?
a : I would. Then I think of an easier clue while putting everything else away. | I know exactly where to find the paper in the morning. My cleverness isn't usually up very early.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like the first snow to come in letters I could read off the sill.
b : What would it spell? | Couldn't you write in it yourself?
a : A question very short and clear. I'd have to guess before the whole sill filled up. | I might put one small line at the side. Snow's own writing deserves the bigger piece.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Waiting tires me more if I can see somebody busy standing still. | I've no patience to spare for a queue kept waiting for no reason.
b : What occupies you while you're waiting?
a : Try to see whether there's some small help nobody's asked for. | See if the next wolf would like a question that isn't about how much longer.

story folded [topic=memories]
  : I tucked a clue into an apple's hollow and gave it to a hurried passer-by.
  : The apple vanished into a pocket and a white corner of paper stayed sticking out.
  b : Did the riddle get solved?
  : By the time the pocket came back I'd thought of three answers. Its owner had thought of a fourth. We ate the evidence.

rule @clue
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Apple first and guessing when you're ready. | Don't squeeze the stalk trying to unfold the paper.

rule @bell
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Evening's got room between its notes. | Plenty of time for one soft answer.
dlg resident.hub : Read the little paper or take the apple and leave it folded.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : At lessons I like a question whose answer gives somebody else a chance to follow with a fresh question.
dlg resident.bye : If your pocket smells sweet you'll remember what's in it.

graft resident.hub
choice What if I can't guess? -> apple_guess
node apple_guess
say Then you eat your apple and I'll keep your question safe till you want it back. Nothing about being puzzled makes a wolf less hungry.
choice What if I guess something else? -> apple_other
choice I'll consider it awhile. -> hub
node apple_other
say Then I've had two good answers for the trouble of writing one riddle. I ought to be wrapping you another apple.
choice I'll consider it awhile. -> hub

grown

line greet : There's a clean place on the board where we can open a thought.
line greet.return : I recognised the quiet before your voice.
line farewell : May the answer find you with something crisp at hand.
line farewell.return : The fold stays yours whether or not you open it.
line decline : A good question gives the other wolf the right to keep quiet.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wrap fruit for a friend without putting an obligation inside.
b : Is there still a clue? | What if a friend won't take presents?
a : If the fruit is welcome. A puzzle that comes with a debt to amuse me isn't much of a gift. | Two clean slices and a request for company can be easier to accept than a parcel.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A riddle with only one possible answer feels a little lonely to me.
b : Won't you say which is right? | How many answers would you allow?
a : I'll say what I had in mind and listen if another answer fits better. | All the ones that give every clue honest work.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Bells take their own time and no shame attaches to a lingering note.
b : Are you comparing a note to a wolf? | Does a prayer have a fixed length?
a : I try to allow a slow friend what I readily allow a piece of ringing metal. | No. I've had one answered before I'd finished finding the words.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take a pause for my jaw when I've been chewing over a troublesome idea too hard.
b : Would you eat an apple then? | Does it bother you physically?
a : Thin slices. I like having a real reason to chew for a change. | A little ache below the ear. My body is remarkably frank about idle fretting.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A clear price tag spares both sides a lot of guessing.
b : Wouldn't a riddle make shopping more interesting? | Suppose the figure's unusually dear?
a : On a separate paper, after the agreement. Food shouldn't vanish behind a clever question. | I can leave it. What I can't choose about is the figure somebody whispers after a parcel's wrapped.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A basket of apples gets sorted more kindly if I turn each one in my palm.
b : Looking for bruises? | Would you keep the smallest?
a : Yes, so a marked apple can be eaten before the hurt goes deeper. | A little one fits a little appetite. I'd sooner keep it than split a grand one for show.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Charcoal makes a kind of quiet grey that I associate with a very particular silence.
b : What does the grey bring back? | Isn't a coal mark dirty?
a : Room enough beside a fire to finish a thought without announcing it to anyone. | On a clean cuff, certainly. On the right paper it's the beginning of a memory.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Snow puts soft wrapping round the city's harder riddles.
b : Does that make them easier? | Which riddle shows clearest?
a : It lets me see where the edges were. With a difficult matter that's often quite enough to begin. | Who has been out early. A set of fresh tracks is an answer with boots on.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a warm rag over a stale heel rather than offer a guest a hard bite in silence.
b : Why keep the hard heel? | Would you say it's yesterday's?
a : For a broth or a bake. Old bread often has more good in it than goes willingly onto a plate. | Yes. I'm trying to soften bread, not the truth about when it left the oven.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like one question for a walk and one clean answer for the way back.
b : What if no answer comes? | Wouldn't company do as well?
a : I've still had the walk. That's more useful than sitting crossly over a folded page. | Company can make the jumbled question feel quite pleasantly small.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a thin week the neatest trick is making a little fruit go round without anybody apologising.
b : Do you cut thinner slices? | Where's the riddle then?
a : I do, and I take a thin one first so no guest need look surprised at the portion. | How a table remembers a whole sweet apple even if each of us got just a piece.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep one easy question for a traveller who looks tired of giving an account.
b : Wouldn't a traveller want rest? | Which question do you ask?
a : Yes. I'd ask whether to leave the folded paper for later before presuming to keep anybody talking. | Which side of an apple has no skin? The inside. A smile's ample answer too.

story smudge [topic=memories]
  : I once smudged a coal-written clue so badly the final word disappeared.
  : I set down three words that might have stood there and tried them out in turn.
  b : Which was the lost word?
  : I couldn't tell. Three perfectly sound riddles came out of my grubby left thumb.

story basket [topic=food]
  : I wrapped an apple in a question and a question in a larger empty wrapper.
  : The baskets got shaken and I had no idea which held supper.
  b : Did you have to open both?
  : I balanced them on my palms. A sound apple still knows more about the answer than a sheet of paper.

rule @patience
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A quiet answer deserves a little elbow room. | Give the fold time to come open on its own.

rule @cold
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The first white scrap's come with no writing on it. | Good light to read small charcoal marks beside a window.
dlg resident.hub : We can leave a little space round your question before answering.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This part came clearly out of its wrapping. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : Keep the thought that tastes best to you.
